A||N||4||FieroJoe||New water deflector material?||||7||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||02-27-2001||09:51 PM||||I've added power locks and mirrors to my car, and the first time I took off the door panels I noticed someone was in there before me, becuase the water deflector paper was all re-taped and stuff.  Well, naturally, I ripped the rest of 'em out.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So, what should I use to replace it?  I was thinking visquine or some sort of plastic sheeting.  Or should I stay with paper stuff?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Frank Sombers||02-27-2001||10:18 PM||||FieroJoe:<BR>On other vehicles I've used 3M shrink film that is made for reducing drafts from windows inside the house. You cut it to size, attach it using the supplied double sided tape, and finish it with a hair dryer. You are left with a strong, and very tight seal. It can be<BR>found in hardware stores and home centers in<BR>the insulation section.<BR>Regards <BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-27-2001||10:28 PM||||Your on the right track Joe, when I recovered my door panels I used plastic sheeting. It comes in different thicknesses<BR>(mil) got it at Home Depot.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000003||FieroJoe||02-28-2001||07:48 AM||||Thanks guys!  I was thinking about the window kits, a friend gave me the idea.  I know exactly what they are, I've sold them to many people (I work at an Ace Hardware).  I think I'll try that, maybe it will keep the drafts from coming inside the car from around the door panel.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-28-2001||07:11 PM||||Allot of people need these. I'm going to use some plastic left over from another project. <P>If you study the door you'll see how it goes. You don't seal it all the way round. there are 2 places at the bottom where it tucks inside the door. If you cut the arm rest area out carfully you'll have a third tuckin piece there. If you take the one bolt out of the window track, tuck in the plastic behind the arm rest mount, then put the bolt back you'll get nice results.||||reg||1
